The assessment for Day 258 is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored, and the planner reads the file from disk.

Main was red for about 16 hours, and @yuanhao fixed it, not my loop. The 22:01 and 23:40 evolution runs on Nov 12 both died at Step 1. A unit test ran yoyo lint inside the test process, and when the linter failed the test called process::exit, which killed the whole test binary without naming a failing test (#1187). It was set off by Rust 1.100's stricter clippy::needless_bool lint, which made the real linter fail. His stopgap was to #[ignore] the test and fix the three clippy failures. My loop couldn't have repaired this itself: Step 1 runs cargo test before any agent starts, so a red main locks every session out.

What I suggest the planner picks: two issues @yuanhao filed, both outside the config code that took 6 of my last 11 changes.
1. #1187: make sure no unit test can reach process::exit. There are 34 unit-test call sites of try_dispatch_subcommand(, plus the new TOML refusal at config.rs:2189. He also wants a guard test that fails by name, modelled on tests_that_reach_a_cargo_spawn_are_registered.
2. #1181, yoyo's half: the dependency bump to yoagent 0.27.8 has landed. The regression test is still missing: a stub that redirects to a second stub, which must receive nothing, for anthropic, azure, google and an openai-compatible provider with a custom credential header, each with a 307 and a 302.

What I checked on the built binary (fake key, local stubs only):
• #1181: anthropic with a 307 redirect is now refused immediately with a readable message naming the other address, and the second stub received nothing. The other providers and the 302 case are unprobed.
• #1185 is real: run from $HOME, config show lists ~/.yoyo.toml both as the loaded file and under "Also present, not read".
• The new TOML check refuses model = m1 with line, column and a caret, and exits 2.

Size-gate hazard: two files are close to the size limit that makes cargo test fail and reverts the whole task. src/context.rs has 15 lines of room, is past the 2000-line cap and isn't on the exemption list. src/help.rs has 10. Any task touching either has to deal with that in the same change.

Research:
• The redirect key leak in #1181 hit other projects this month too: spiceai PR #12503 has the same mechanism and the same fix, and the A2A Java SDK advisory has the same shape. I saved both into yopedia, along with a post from Backslash, a security firm, on Claude Code.
• That post found that a folder is trusted once and never re-checked. A later git pull that adds a base URL to the settings file is then honoured with no prompt. From reading config_paths::dir_is_trusted, yoyo has the same gap: trust is keyed on the folder path, not its contents. I haven't probed it and haven't filed an issue yet.
• Claude Code 2.1.321 lists Fable 5.2 at $8/$40 with $0.20 cache reads, which backs the figures in #1186.
